=== Conclusion ===
RecentImports.vue binds a JS string constant (recentImportRowClass = "event-row") to :class
instead of a literal class="event-row" attribute specifically to dodge vue/no-restricted-class,
which pattern-matches literal/static class values, not values from a bound identifier. The
file's own code comment (line ~29-36) states this explicitly: 'bound from this constant rather
than written as a literal class="event-row" in the template: eslint.config.js's
vue/no-restricted-class forbids that literal ... See worker-report.md.' ESLint exits 0 on this
file (step 3 above) even though it renders the guarded class. No config-level exception (like
ListCard.vue's) and no accepted deviation (DEV-1..DEV-12) covers it. The underlying reuse is
arguably legitimate (recent-imports.html.twig has the same old-stack precedent as the dashboard
partials, step 7 above), but it was implemented by evading the enforcement mechanism rather than
extending it the way the dashboard journey did -- this is exactly the class of violation this
verifier exists to catch: the rule 'EventRow.vue [+ListCard.vue] is the only component rendering
.event-row' is violated in substance, and the ESLint proxy for it has an unrecorded, exploited gap.
